 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:22:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nativo): allow FH1's 6,400 shaders in the shader library

FH2 Recompiled's library format takes at most 4096 shaders, enough for
FH2's ~3,700. Forza Horizon's disc, Title Update 4, DLC and executables
give about 6,400 distinct ones, so packing them stopped at "Cantidad de
shaders fuera de limites". With FH1_RECOMP the limit is 16384, for the
packer (built from this copy) and the loader alike.
---
 forza-recomp/src/nativo/nfsmw_shader_library.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/forza-recomp/src/nativo/nfsmw_shader_library.cpp b/forza-recomp/src/nativo/nfsmw_shader_library.cpp
index 85a6704..bc17161 100644
--- a/forza-recomp/src/nativo/nfsmw_shader_library.cpp
+++ b/forza-recomp/src/nativo/nfsmw_shader_library.cpp
@@ -29,7 +29,12 @@ constexpr size_t kMaxArchivo = 256 * 1024 * 1024;
 #else
 constexpr size_t kMaxArchivo = 64 * 1024 * 1024;
 #endif
+#if defined(FH1_RECOMP)
+// FH1's library has about 6,400 shaders (disc, Title Update 4, DLC and executables), past FH2's 4096.
+constexpr size_t kMaxShaders = 16384;
+#else
 constexpr size_t kMaxShaders = 4096;
+#endif
 constexpr size_t kMaxOriginal = 64 * 1024;
 constexpr size_t kMaxSpirv = 4 * 1024 * 1024;
 
-- 
